            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hey,\r\n\r\nCuriously I have the same issue. I've updated drivers and installed both through Conda, and manually as suggested above. it still gives me the same error:\r\nI do activate my environments before testing.\r\n\r\n`CREATING-SOME LABELS FOR THE FRAMES                                                                                                                         Traceback (most recent call last):                                                                                                                            File \"testscript.py\", line 108, in <module>                                                                                                                   dataFrame.to_hdf(                                                                                                                                         File \"C:\\Users\\phar0732\\.conda\\envs\\DEEPLABCUT2\\lib\\site-packages\\pandas\\core\\generic.py\", line 2703, in to_hdf                                               pytables.to_hdf(                                                                                                                                          File \"C:\\Users\\phar0732\\.conda\\envs\\DEEPLABCUT2\\lib\\site-packages\\pandas\\io\\pytables.py\", line 311, in to_hdf                                                 with HDFStore(                                                                                                                                            File \"C:\\Users\\phar0732\\.conda\\envs\\DEEPLABCUT2\\lib\\site-packages\\pandas\\io\\pytables.py\", line 572, in __init__                                               tables = import_optional_dependency(\"tables\")                                                                                                             File \"C:\\Users\\phar0732\\.conda\\envs\\DEEPLABCUT2\\lib\\site-packages\\pandas\\compat\\_optional.py\", line 118, in import_optional_dependency                        raise ImportError(msg) from None                                                                                                                        ImportError: Missing optional dependency 'tables'.  Use pip or conda to install tables.        `\r\n\r\nI assume this will be dealt with using docker, but it is weird that that same thing occurs and it does not appear to be that common. Really wonder where this conflict between tables pytables and pandas arise from and how it is so random...",
